038 #edb/ref 17592186269133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186367429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186483345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1039 "Constructing the Normal Equation Corresponding to a Linear System" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186133634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "fda08f5d-4513-5be0-b8c4-475e82f9bf5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1045 "The Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System (With Collinearity)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186134698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1050 1200.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "dac16d4a-58b8-5e9c-b569-e42a4c036b80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134333 #edb/ref 1069 "q-40943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134333 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134333 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ shown above. If the general least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+2b+c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134333 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "871a1be1-8f4a-5616-a788-c400e98cd9b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134333 #edb/ref 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 12 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 12 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -8 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{2}+{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}-4(\\frac{3}{2}+{x}_{3})+2{x}_{3}=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2+{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2+{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+2b+c=1+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}+0=4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134698 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134698 #edb/ref 1061 20272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134698 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "73e4890e-8287-5a80-8c3c-2c95ce05512e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134698 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186135060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134699 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134699 #edb/ref 1061 20273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134699 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2664b077-4f38-5154-af4c-d4fd21596b27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134699 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134700 #edb/ref 1061 20275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134700 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f4594719-c6f8-53f5-bc1a-22e17b863c14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134700 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134733 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134733 #edb/ref 1061 22147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134733 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a43860da-1a59-5a1c-930e-23d6f893c13a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134733 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135060 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider the following inconsistent system of equations:\n\n![](images/6b/6bcdc34077d88eac5ed89d408a1d2525b617a4f427b13433757df918585d380f.svg)\n\nSince the system is inconsistent, we cannot find an exact solution. However, as we've previously seen, we can attempt to find the so-called least-squares solution, which is a vector ${\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\|  A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}} - \\mathbf{b} \\|\n$$\n\nis as small as possible. \n\nAs before, the least-squares solution can be found by solving the corresponding normal equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, note the following: \n\n- Previously, we solved the normal equation by left-multiplying the normal equation by $(A^T A)^{-1}.$\n\n- However, in this case, the second column of $A$ is a multiple of the first.\n\n- So, the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent.\n\n- Therefore, $A^T A$ is not invertible.\n\nTo solve the normal equation in this case, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5 & -20 \\\\ -20 & 80\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the last equation by Gaussian elimination, we obtain the general solution\n\n![](images/b9/b93bd5cb988f208eb26115bfaa08e81be989ee79cf3655612c1a0522a5566d95.svg)\n\nNotice that our solution is not unique! The second term of the least-squares solution (highlighted in blue) represents vectors from the null space of $A.$ \n\nIn general, if a matrix $A$ has collinear columns, then the least-squares solution to $A\\mathbf x = \\mathbf b$ is not unique." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135060 #edb/ref 1065 3637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135060 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2f2e227a-264e-5e00-8c12-ea534f4b351f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135060 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267142 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267142 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267142 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "71872f14-7cc4-5fb9-8cf7-9ffe96aefe19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267146 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267146 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267146 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "725897a0-9e77-57f9-b8a9-68f56715093b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267158 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267158 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267158 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7360267e-e517-562f-a7ab-234dea8e16b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267291 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267291 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267291 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "828574ad-8b28-58c3-ac93-daffbb878a55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267380 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267380 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267380 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8a852bda-8769-55af-b974-271e085d782f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267556 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267556 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267556 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9d160852-1af1-56d1-8d23-a808bbfc6b00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267694 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267694 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267694 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "abc3d198-0e91-5133-9e31-d766dcdd7bac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268116 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 175921860